<title>LEBANON: Lebanon public debt up 5.45 pct in Jan-Feb-Assoc.</title>
<headline>Lebanon public debt up 5.45 pct in Jan-Feb-Assoc.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's public debt rose by 5.45 percent in the first two months of 1997, according to figures issued by the Lebanese Banks Association on Thursday.</p>
<p>The cumulative deficit of income to expenditure rose to 52.3 percent in February from 50.4 percent in January. It was 51.5 at the end of December 1996, the association said.</p>
<p>The association issued the following details of Lebanon's public finances (billions of Lebanese pounds at end of period unless otherwise stated):</p>
<p>		    Dec 96   Jan 97   Feb 97    Dec 96/Feb 97</p>
<p>Revenues</p>
<p>(Cumulative)    3,532	250	515</p>
<p>monthly change		 250	265</p>
<p>Expenses</p>
<p>(Cumulative)    7,288	504    1,079</p>
<p>Monthly change		 504	575</p>
<p>Deficit</p>
<p>(Cumulative)    3,756	254	564</p>
<p>Monthly change		 254	310</p>
<p>Deficit/</p>
<p>expenses	  51.5%     50.4%    52.3%</p>
<p>Monthly change		0.01     0.02</p>
<p>Total debt     20,070   20,766    21,163    5.45%</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057</p>
</text>
